review_comments.body:
`_build_s3_client()` always passes `aws_access_key_id` / `aws_secret_access_key` from settings even when they’re empty strings. This prevents boto3’s default credential provider chain (env/shared config/IAM role) from working and can break production deployments where credentials aren’t explicitly set. Build `kwargs` so credentials are only included when non-empty (and consider supporting session tokens).
```suggestion
    kwargs: dict = {
        "service_name": "s3",
    }
    if settings.AWS_REGION:
        kwargs["region_name"] = settings.AWS_REGION

    access_key = getattr(settings, "AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID", None)
    secret_key = getattr(settings, "AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY", None)
    session_token = getattr(settings, "AWS_SESSION_TOKEN", None)

    if access_key and secret_key:
        kwargs["aws_access_key_id"] = access_key
        kwargs["aws_secret_access_key"] = secret_key
        if session_token:
            kwargs["aws_session_token"] = session_token
```
